# Docs editing rules

Follow `docs/meta/documentation-standards.md`.

## Must

- Put content in the correct folder by maturity and topic (`ideas/` until confirmed).
- Add YAML status front matter on content docs: `draft` | `active` | `deprecated`.
- Use kebab-case English filenames; one primary topic per file.
- Mark unknowns with TBD or `## Open questions` — do not invent lore/systems/plot to fill gaps.
- When promoting from `ideas/`, update or deprecate the old file and refresh folder indexes.
- Keep `docs/vision/` and root `README.md` in sync when premise/themes change.

## Must not

- Create a separate docs repository or move the design bible outside this repo.
- Leave lasting contradictions between `active` docs; resolve by editing.
- Dump chat transcripts into `docs/` — distill conclusions instead.
